1
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:25,199
This will be one crazy weekend.

2
00:06:38,399 --> 00:06:44,399
Sawed Off is a horror film directed by Hunter Johnson.

3
00:09:57,599 --> 00:10:03,599
The movie centers on two hunters, friends for years and vying for the affections of the same woman,
who find themselves on cursed land and keep killing each other and coming back to life.

4
00:13:16,799 --> 00:13:22,799
Marjorie, played by Eva Hamilton.

5
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Frank, played by Trae Ireland.

6
00:19:55,199 --> 00:20:01,199
Jon, played by Jody Barton.

7
00:23:14,399 --> 00:23:20,399
Saw is a 2004 American psychological horror thriller film directed by James Wan in his feature
directorial debut, and written by Leigh Whannell, from a story by Wan and Whannell.

8
00:26:33,599 --> 00:26:39,599
It stars Whannell alongside Cary Elwes, Danny Glover,
Monica Potter, Michael Emerson, and Ken Leung.

9
00:29:52,799 --> 00:29:58,799
The film tells a nonlinear narrative revolving around the mystery of the Jigsaw Killer, who tests his victims' will to live by
putting them through deadly "games" where they must inflict great physical pain upon themselves to survive.

10
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:18,000
The frame story follows Jigsaw's latest victims (Whannell and Elwes), who awaken in a large,
dilapidated bathroom, with one being ordered to kill the other to save his own family.

11
00:36:31,199 --> 00:36:37,199
The screenplay was written by Whannell, who co-created the story
with Wan in their respective screenwriting debuts.

12
00:39:50,399 --> 00:39:56,399
The film was originally written in 2001, but after failed attempts to get the script produced in Wan
and Whannell's home country of Australia, they were urged to travel to Los Angeles.

13
00:43:09,599 --> 00:43:15,599
In order to help attract producers, they shot a low-budget short
film of the same name from a scene out of the script.

14
00:46:28,799 --> 00:46:34,799
This proved successful in 2003 as producers were immediately attached and
also formed a horror genre production label, Twisted Pictures.

15
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:54,000
The film was given a small production budget and was shot in 18 days.

16
00:53:07,199 --> 00:53:13,199
Saw was first screened at the 2004 Sundance Film Festival on January 19, 2004.

17
00:56:26,399 --> 00:56:32,399
Due to positive audience reception, Lions Gate picked up
the distribution rights for the film.

18
00:59:45,599 --> 00:59:51,599
Originally planned for a straight-to-video release, they decided to instead
release the film in theaters in North America on October 29, 2004.

19
01:03:04,799 --> 01:03:10,799
The film received mixed reviews from critics.

20
01:06:24,000 --> 01:06:30,000
After topping the opening weekend box office, the film would go on to gross $104 million
worldwide to become one of the most profitable horror films since Scream (1996).

21
01:09:43,199 --> 01:09:49,199
The success of Saw launched a media franchise, including several
sequels, video games, theme park rides, and merchandising.

22
01:13:02,399 --> 01:13:08,399
The first sequel, titled Saw II, was released the
following year in October 2005.

23
01:16:21,599 --> 01:16:27,599
The film explores themes of hunter, ancient curse, cursed land.

24
01:19:40,799 --> 01:19:46,799
The tone is dark.
